= denouement
~ location_name = "VDénouement"
~ violence_count += 1
# CLEAR

Elvis Christian (a.k.a. "The King") had been trucking for over 20 years until that day.  The day he walked into the Jersey Tasty Freeze and got into an argument.  A Coors-infused, heated dispute over the proper ingredients of frozen custard.  He didn't mean to push the server, but it happened.  She fell and ended up paralyzed.  His life in tatters.  10 years later, Elvis is an ex-con, released on parole with ill-conceived dreams of revenge sitting cozily on the chip of his expansive shoulder.

Delivering Busch Lite to an uptown dive, "The King" blinked, wiped his eyes and blinked again.  Thomas Howard, Tasty Freeze CEO existing "L'Aura", less than a block away thumbing for a cab.  The decision was instant (well as instant as Elvis could ever be) and autonomous.  He accelerated, lining up Howard with a crack in his windshield.  "He had it coming", Elvis convinced himself.  It would only be the second time he had seriously broken the law, but the notion of law no longer held any sway over him.  A common side effect of troubled incarcerations. 

Out of nowhere, a stray dog darts into the street.  "Peaches," the family dog of his youth, screams Elvis!  No longer able to stop his ton and a half projectile, he swerves violently to the right, narrowly missing the dog... 

The panel truck missile flashes into Mille's vision as she considered possible titles for her article.  Too fast she was thinking, too late to react. Too brutal.  A simple Haiku was the last thing in Mille's mind as she fell, making fatal contact with the cold, hard fall NYC concrete.

# CLASS: computer
Entropy of dust,<br>Boredom drags me to my grave,<br>Final breath is drawn.

